  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 302 AM CDT Sat Sep 12 2026\n\nThe LREF has an upper high building across the southern CONUS early \nnext week which will brings the front back north across the CWA on \nMonday keeping a chance of showers and thunderstorms across the \narea.  This will also puts us into southwest flow aloft Tuesday and \nWednesday which will keeps a cold front stalled across northern \nparts of Missouri and Illinois. The 850mb temperatures are \nforecast to climb back to around 20C with southwesterly surface \nwinds behind the warm front supporting highs back into the 80s \nand 90s. This is supported by the NBM IQR at St. Louis which has\nhighs in the mid 90s on Tuesday and Wednesday with a spread of \nonly 3 degrees. This spread increases late next week as the \nupper high retrogrades which will allow the upper flow to become\nzonal which brings into question where the surface front will \nbe Thursday into Friday. 30-60% of the LREF members are \nproducing rain over the CWA Thursday into Friday. Temperatures \nwill also begin to drop off closer to normal with the front and \nrain chances.",
